        <mxCell id="openitems" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=9;spacing=6;dashed=1;fontStyle=2;" value="OPEN ITEMS (v2, updated — confirmed via code review of cc-fee-service and fee-processor):&#xa;- Steps 19-23 (Credit Card Transactions Service through Fiserv Optis Partner) remain UNVERIFIED — no code has been reviewed for this service; shown as previously mapped from the original architect diagram / meeting transcript only.&#xa;- Return Payments Processor ALSO has a confirmed, real Kafka listener on CC_ACCOUNT_ALL_FEE (FeeTransactionKafkaConsumer) that is not shown as a distinct step here — whether it ever receives more than the single initial REQUESTED-status message published at step 17a is UNRESOLVED. This is the key remaining gap in understanding how (or whether) Return Payments Processor ever learns the fee&#39;s FINAL settled status.&#xa;- Step 10 (GET /fees) hits the same query gap discussed separately with the accounts team: the default filter requires current_status=POSTED AND transaction_status IN (BILLED, UNBILLED) — and fee-processor&#39;s real-time status pipeline cannot produce that exact combination on its own (see Fee_Status_Lifecycle_StateChart_v1). UNBILLED is only set via a DMON-type event whose true source is still unconfirmed.&#xa;- The eligibility gate at steps 1-2 now reflects the proposed redesign (JAMS-triggered, cycle-date-gated) agreed with Oleg/Arvil Wright, replacing the original event-driven trigger shown in the architect&#39;s source diagram — this is a DESIGN CHANGE, not yet implemented, tracked separately from SSPP-11614.&#xa;- feeCategory whitelist (step 16) currently only allows EXPRESS_PAYMENT_FEE in code; adding RETURNED_PAYMENT_FEE is an in-progress fix on the cc-fee-service side, separate from any JSON-schema-only ticket." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="3900" x="40" y="1030" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
